.TH RFIND.CONF 5 "2026-10-14" "rfind 0.7.0" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
rfind.conf \- configuration of the rfindd indexing daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I /etc/rfindd/config.toml
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR rfindd (8)
reads its configuration from a TOML file, written with the defaults on its
first start.
Every setting is optional.
Unknown keys are an error, so a typo can't silently change behavior; check
the file with
.BR "rfind config check" .
.PP
The file can be edited by hand (then run
.BR "rfind reload" )
or changed with
.BR "rfind config" ,
which keeps comments, validates every change and reloads the daemon; see
.BR rfind (1).
All paths must be absolute.
.SH [scan]
.TP
.BR roots " (list of paths; default " [\(dq/\(dq] )
Live roots: scanned, then kept current by fanotify or inotify.
.TP
.BR exclude " (list of paths; default " /proc ", " /sys ", " /dev ", " /run ", " /media )
Paths never indexed and never descended into, with everything below them.
.TP
.BR workers " (integer; default " 0 )
Scanner threads;
.B 0
means one per CPU.
.TP
.BR reindex_interval_hours " (integer; default " 6 )
Full rescan of the live roots when the last one is older than this at
startup, and periodically in index-only mode.
.B 0
disables it.
.TP
.BR collect_mtime " (boolean; default " true )
Record modification times and file sizes.
Without them,
.BR "rfind recent" ,
.BR "rfind size" ,
.B rfind largest
and the size filters have nothing to work with; scanning is slightly faster.
.TP
.BR io_uring " (boolean; default " true )
Batch the scanner's
.BR statx (2)
calls through
.BR io_uring (7).
About twice as fast on local disks and network filesystems; rfindd falls
back to plain system calls when io_uring is unavailable.
.SS [[scan.periodic_roots]]
One table per root that is rescanned on an interval instead of monitored.
A periodic root inside a live root is skipped by the live root's scans.
.TP
.B path
The root.
.TP
.BR interval_hours " (integer; default " 12 )
Hours between rescans;
.B 0
scans only once.
.SH [index]
.TP
.BR db_path " (path; default " /var/lib/rfindd/index.db )
The index database.
.TP
.BR batch_size " (integer; default " 10000 )
Entries per scanner write transaction.
.TP
.BR compress " (boolean; default " true )
Store the index with zstd-compressed pages, about 3 times smaller.
Searches and live updates work the same; the database file itself becomes
an empty stub next to
.I index.db-zdata.*
and
.I index.db-zmap
files.
Changing this setting rebuilds the index.
.SH [monitor]
.TP
.BR prefer_fanotify " (boolean; default " true )
Use fanotify (one mark per filesystem; Linux 5.9+) when possible.
.TP
.BR inotify_fallback " (boolean; default " true )
Fall back to per-directory inotify watches when fanotify is unavailable.
With both disabled or unavailable, rfindd rescans the live roots every
.B reindex_interval_hours
hours.
.TP
.BR watch_new_mounts " (boolean; default " true )
Index and watch filesystems mounted under a live root after startup.
Overlay and pseudo filesystems and bind mounts of indexed files are ignored.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
# Index the whole system; Windows drives are rescanned twice a day.
[scan]
roots = ["/"]
exclude = [
    "/proc",
    "/sys",
    "/dev",
    "/run",
    "/media",
    "/home/moshe",
]
workers = 0
reindex_interval_hours = 6
collect_mtime = true
io_uring = true

[[scan.periodic_roots]]
path = "/mnt/c"
interval_hours = 12

[index]
db_path = "/var/lib/rfindd/index.db"
batch_size = 10000
compress = true

[monitor]
prefer_fanotify = true
inotify_fallback = true
watch_new_mounts = true
.fi
.SH NOTES
Under WSL2, put Windows drives
.RI ( /mnt/c ", " /mnt/d ", ...)"
in
.B periodic_roots
or
.BR exclude :
changes made from Windows produce no kernel events.
rfindd logs a warning for a Windows drive under a live root.
Network filesystems (NFS, SMB) belong in
.B periodic_roots
for the same reason.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/rfindd/config.toml
The configuration.
The
.B RFIND_CONFIG
environment variable selects another file for both
.B rfind
and
.BR rfindd .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rfind (1),
.BR rfindd (8)
